{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>For we went up to your servant my father and told him the words of my lord.</b> He said that when they came to him, they immediately told him that they would not see his face again without their youngest brother, and he was unwilling to send him, and he left Simeon in his imprisonment. And this is the meaning of \"our father said, Go back, buy us a little food,\" for he did not want to agree to send him for all that we said until the famine pressed him."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:44:38.206381345Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}